{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'rg -n \"real-agent|real agent|WORK_LEAF_REAL_AGENT_OK|codex --cd|feature done|Is this feature done|yes/no|verification|visible result|pre-agent\" -S .'","aggregated_output":"./AGENTS.md:100:Every patch must include a real-agent verification step before it is marked ready. Automated tests\n./AGENTS.md:107:during implementation. The ready report must state the exact real-agent scenario that was run and the\n./AGENTS.md:108:user-visible result. If the patch does not affect any agent-facing behavior, the ready report must\n./AGENTS.md:109:state that no real-agent workflow is affected and explain why.\n./AGENTS.md:111:Review agents must treat missing real-agent verification as a finding for agent-facing changes.\n./AGENTS.md:115:### Real Codex verification troubleshooting\n./AGENTS.md:122:printf 'Reply exactly with WORK_LEAF_REAL_AGENT_OK and do not modify files.\\n' | \\\n./AGENTS.md:123:  codex --cd \"$PWD\" --sandbox read-only --ask-for-approval never \\\n./AGENTS.md:142:When real Codex verification is blocked by local Codex initialization or auth-state isolation, the\n./AGENTS.md:143:ready report must say exactly which command was attempted, which pre-agent error occurred, and which\n./AGENTS.md:144:automated tests cover the behavior instead. A blocked real-agent smoke check is not a green\n./AGENTS.md:145:real-agent verification.\n./src/workspace.rs:18:pub(crate) const FEATURE_DONE_PROMPT: &str = \"work-leaf: Is this feature done? yes/no\";\n./tests/terminal_app.rs:1095:            .contains(\"work-leaf: Is this feature done? yes/no\")\n./src/linearize.rs:200:7. Report the final commit messages, removed provisional messages, grouping decisions, and verification results.\\n\\\n./src/linearize.rs:265:    prompt.push_str(\"\\nIterate until the verification commands pass. Keep the resulting history minimal and coherent for human review.\\n\");\n./tests/workspace.rs:353:            .any(|line| line == \"work-leaf: Is this feature done? yes/no\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
